            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> @igorlfs could you try this locally and LMK if it feels right?\r\n\r\nMy first impression is that it looks odd, but I guess that's because the underlying nvim instance is not using my colorscheme. Its (i.e, the window's) size was also larger than what I expected.\r\n\r\nExperimenting a little more, I ran into some quirks:\r\n- When I press `<C-c>` (inside the `cmdwin`), the window is gone, and it's replaced with \"blank space\". It remains there until I press some other key.\r\n- I'm not sure if that's easier with one my mappings, but I managed to delete the temporary file with some combination of `<ESC>` (mapped to `<C-\\><C-n>` in terminal mode), `<C-[` and `<C-c>` (I assume the specifics are not really important now). This state leaves the terminal window here, until it's manually closed. In fact, I can start a second \"input session\" and the window is not overridden.\r\n\r\nOf course, these were attempts to find limitations with the current implementation. For the next few days I'll daily drive this and I'll be back with some \"real usage\" opinions.",
