            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": ">  the window's size was also larger than what I expected\r\n\r\nThis has some weird side effects. If the operation that triggered the input depends on the current line number, it may change unexpectedly. Example: with nvim-dap, using `vim.ui.input` (or `vim.fn.input`) to set a conditional breakpoint on a line that's at the bottom of the screen. The breakpoint will be set  on the upper half of the window. However, **this only happens when there's more than 1 window in the current tab**. Demo:\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82e8b5d3-856d-4b26-9ee2-e8fb208957ce\r\n\r\n",
